# Product Requirements Document (PRD)

## Project Overview

**Name:** Rakesh Dry Cleaners

**Description:** A premium digital experience for Rakesh Dry Cleaners that showcases garment care, transparent pricing, and a unified booking workflow. Combines immersive brand storytelling (scroll-driven canvas sequence) with practical service selection, scheduling, and a WhatsApp confirmation.

**Platform:** Next.js 14 (App Router) web application

**Stack:** React 18, TypeScript, Next.js App Router, ESLint, Vitest + Testing Library. No CSS framework (hand-written CSS in `app/globals.css`).

## Purpose

Provide a polished marketing and booking interface for a local dry cleaning provider. The site should:

- Showcase core service offerings (Wash, Wash & Iron, Dry Clean, Colour Restore, Rafoo / Mending)
- Present pricing clearly and visually
- Let customers select service items, quantities, and schedule collection or drop-off
- Display a live order summary with estimated totals
- Let users contact the business quickly (call, email, maps, WhatsApp)
- Support responsive layouts and accessible interactions
- Support English, Marathi, and Hindi through a client-side language switcher

## Goals

- Convert visitors into bookings via a clear service discovery and scheduling flow
- Build trust through testimonials, service pillars, and operational details
- Keep the experience fast and engaging with scroll-driven visuals and progressive loading
- Make interaction accessible on desktop and mobile

## Target Users

- Local residents who need laundry, dry cleaning, mending, and fabric restoration
- Customers looking for easy scheduling, transparent pricing, and quick WhatsApp booking
- Mobile users who want to book on their phone

## User Stories

- As a customer, I can browse service categories to understand what is offered.
- As a customer, I can view pricing for items so I can estimate cost.
- As a customer, I can pick items and quantities to build an order.
- As a customer, I can schedule collection/drop-off by choosing a date and time.
- As a customer, I can review a summary of my order before confirming.
- As a customer, I can contact the shop through phone, email, maps, or a floating WhatsApp button.
- As a customer, I can read the site in English, Marathi, or Hindi.

## Product Scope

### Core Features

1. Hero scroll experience
   - Preload a 300-frame image set
   - Render a canvas sequence matched to scroll position
   - Show dynamic copy beats with progress-based storytelling
   - Snap frames instead of interpolating when `prefers-reduced-motion` is set
   - Use a mobile-sized frame set on small screens

2. Service discovery
   - Five service categories: Wash, Wash & Iron, Dry Clean, Colour Restore, Rafoo (Mending)
   - Descriptions and example coverage areas
   - Quick Book-now CTA on each card that preselects the matching booking tab

3. Booking workflow
   - Category tabs (five categories)
   - Sub-category filters (Tops & Shirts, Bottoms, Formal & Outerwear, Ethnic & Traditional, Home & Bedding, Dress)
   - Pricing item list with quantity controls
   - Live order summary sidebar with item count and estimated total
   - Date and time selection
   - Optional pickup address and special instructions
   - Confirm booking via a pre-filled WhatsApp message

4. Contact and trust
   - Address, phone, email, working hours
   - Google Maps embed modal and external maps link
   - Testimonials and trust stats
   - Four pillars of fabric care

5. Navigation and i18n
   - Responsive top navigation with scrollspy and accessible mobile menu
   - Language switcher (English / मराठी / हिंदी), persisted in `localStorage`

### Out of Scope

- Order tracking UI
- Backend APIs or a database
- Light/dark theme toggle
- Server-side payments

## UI Sections

- Loading screen
- Navigation bar (with language switcher)
- Main scroll sequence
- Services section
- Booking section with pricing, scheduling, and order summary sidebar
- Testimonials and trust stats
- Fabric care pillars
- Contact section
- Footer
- WhatsApp floating button
- Map embed modal

## Pricing and Service Details

### Service Categories (starting prices)

- Wash — ₹180
- Wash & Iron — ₹250
- Dry Clean — ₹300
- Colour Restore — ₹700
- Rafoo (Mending) — ₹120

### Pricing Items

Item-level pricing is defined in `lib/service-data.ts` (`SERVICE_ITEMS`) and surfaced through the booking workflow with quantity controls and an estimated total. Full item lists:

- Wash: T-Shirt ₹200, Shirt ₹180, Polo T-Shirt ₹220, Jeans ₹280, Shorts ₹150, Pyjama ₹160, Kurta ₹300, Salwar Suit ₹350, Bedsheet ₹400, Pillow Cover ₹100, Curtain (per panel) ₹500, Sofa Cover (per seat) ₹600, Car Seat Cover ₹550, School Dress ₹250, Casual Dress ₹320
- Wash & Iron: Shirt ₹350, T-Shirt ₹260, Formal Shirt ₹380, Trousers ₹250, Jeans ₹320, Skirt ₹280, Kurta ₹340, Kurta Pyjama Set ₹480, Salwar Suit ₹420, Bedsheet ₹450, Pillow Cover ₹130, Sundress ₹400, School Dress ₹300
- Dry Clean: Formal Shirt ₹450, Trousers ₹420, Blazer ₹900, 2-Piece Suit ₹1600, 3-Piece Suit ₹2000, Winter Coat ₹1200, Jacket ₹850, Waistcoat ₹400, Tie ₹150, Saree ₹650, Sherwani ₹1100, Lehenga ₹1500, Dupatta ₹300, Blanket/Quilt ₹700, Carpet/Rug (small) ₹800, Sofa Cover (per seat) ₹750, Car Seat Cover ₹700, Evening Gown ₹950, Frock ₹500
- Colour Restore: Shirt ₹800, T-Shirt ₹700, Trousers ₹750, Jeans ₹780, Blazer ₹1100, Kurta ₹820, Saree ₹950, Evening Gown ₹1050
