All item labels render from the translation dictionaries (`item.*` keys), not from the data module.

## Functional Requirements

### User Journey

1. User arrives on the homepage.
2. Loading screen displays until the 300-frame hero sequence is preloaded.
3. User sees navigation, hero storytelling, and sections.
4. User scrolls to services and inspects the offerings.
5. User clicks a service card or a booking tab to pick a category.
6. User selects items, adjusts quantities, and reviews pricing.
7. User chooses a date, time, and optional address/instructions.
8. The order summary shows item count, collection details, and estimated total.
9. User confirms, which opens a pre-filled WhatsApp message.
10. User can contact the shop via phone, email, Google Maps, or the WhatsApp button.

### i18n

- All copy resolves through `t('namespace.key')` from `lib/translations.ts` (`en`/`mr`/`hi`).
- The active language is read from `localStorage` (`kdc:lang`) after mount and written on change.
- `document.documentElement.lang` and `document.title` sync with the active language.
- Translation dictionaries are enforced to have identical key sets by a test.

### Accessibility

- Skip-to-content link included.
- Keyboard-navigable tabs (arrow keys / Home / End on category and sub-category tabs), cards, and buttons.
- ARIA roles and labels on major interactive groups and modals.
- Respects `prefers-reduced-motion` for the scroll sequence and WhatsApp pulse.

### Responsive Behavior

- Mobile navigation drawer with action buttons.
- Sequence uses mobile-optimized frames (`public/frames-mobile`) on smaller screens.
- Layout stacks on mobile and uses grids on desktop.

### Performance

- Preload hero frames and delay the main sequence until ready.
- Draw the sequence on a canvas to keep playback smooth.
- Loading screen falls back after a timeout if frame loading stalls.

## Technical Architecture

### Files and Components

- `app/layout.tsx` — metadata, `LanguageProvider`, `WhatsAppButton`.
- `app/page.tsx` — page sections, service catalog, map modal, booking state.
- `components/Navbar.tsx` — navigation, scrollspy, language switcher, mobile menu.
- `components/SequenceCanvas.tsx` — frame preloading and scroll-driven canvas rendering.
- `components/LoadingScreen.tsx` — progress overlay driven by `kdc:loadprogress`.
- `components/BookingClient.tsx` — tabs, item picker, scheduling, order summary, WhatsApp confirm.
- `components/CardFlip.tsx`, `components/WhatsAppButton.tsx`, `components/LanguageSwitcher.tsx`.
- `lib/i18n.tsx` — i18n provider/context and `useI18n` hook.
- `lib/translations.ts` — `en` / `mr` / `hi` dictionaries.
- `lib/service-data.ts` — categories, pricing items, time slots, date helpers.
- `app/globals.css` — global styles and design tokens.
- `public/frames`, `public/frames-mobile`, `public/Services` — static assets.

### External Dependencies

- `next` — framework and routing
- `react`, `react-dom` — UI library and DOM renderer
- Dev/test: `vitest`, `@testing-library/react`, `@testing-library/user-event`, `@testing-library/jest-dom`, `jsdom`, `typescript`, `eslint`, `eslint-config-next`

## Deployment

- Build with `npm run build`, serve with `npm run start`.
- Host on Vercel or any Node-compatible platform supporting Next.js.

## Future Enhancements

- Real backend API for bookings and order tracking.
- Database-backed bookings with automatic confirmations.
- Search/filter within service pricing.
- Multiple cities, pickup zones, and dynamic pricing.
- Light/dark theme support.
